cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "RepoAuditor: evidence-bounded security review for acquired codebases"
abstract: >-
  A security-review pipeline for acquired codebases that combines deterministic scanners,
  bounded architecture and trust-boundary analysis, human-reviewed findings, quantitative
  evidence summaries, and separate engineering and leadership reports. Scanner matches and
  model outputs are treated as review candidates rather than proof of exploitability.
type: software
authors:
  - name: erxxc
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-10"
repository-code: "https://github.com/erxxc/repoauditor"
url: "https://github.com/erxxc/repoauditor"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - application security
  - software composition analysis
  - static analysis
  - code audit
  - vulnerability triage
  - security evidence
  - weak random number generation
references:
